==Points of Interest==
===Fighting Dojo===
In the north-east of the city is a dojo. By defeating the Karate Master there, the player will receive a reward choice of a Hitmonlee, Hitmonchan or Hitmontop.

After collecting the reward, behind it the player will then find the [[Type Experts|Fighting Type Expert]].

===Silph Co. Head Office===
In the middle of the city is [[Silph Co. Head Office]]. When the player first visits the city, Team Rocket are in control of the city, preventing access to many locations. To clear out Team Rocket, the player must defeat them in Silph Co.

===Restaurant===
In the south-west of the city is a Restaurant. After Team Rocket has been cleared out, the player can receive a Fancy Meal there daily for free, and purchase additional Fancy Meals for ₽500 each. While Team Rocket are still in control of the city, if the player is wearing a Team Rocket outfit, they can instead receive a Rocket Meal each day.

The Fossil Maniac can also be found in the restaurant after defeating him in [[Celadon City]]. This time after defeating him, he will give the player a choice of a {{ItemIcon|JAWFOSSIL}} Jaw Fossil or a {{ItemIcon|SAILFOSSIL}} Sail Fossil.

===Train Station===
The train station in the north-west of the city allows the player to quickly travel to [[Goldenrod City]]. To take the train, the player must purchase a ticket for ₽1,000.

===Bar===
On the western edge of the city is a bar where the player can complete several quests. The bouncer in front of the door will only allow the player in during the [[Time|day]]. Certain events however can only be done during the night; so the player must wait in the bathroom until night (an NPC there allow the player to skip in hour at a time).

===Boutique===
In the building to the southeast of the Poké Mart is the Saffron Boutique where the player can receive and purchase a variety of [[Character Customization|character customization items]]. The vendor behind the bottom-left counter will sell dye kits which allow the player to change the color of their outfits. The woman by the left salon chair will sell some exclusive Pokémon-inspired [[List of Hair Styles|haircuts]]. The woman by the right salon chair will randomize the player's outfit. The fashion designer on the runway will create [[List of Hats|hats]] and [[List of Clothes|clothes]] inspired by the species of Pokémon that the player shows them.

===Individual Value Analyser===
[[File:Individual Values Analyser Machine.png|thumb|Individual Values Analyzer Machine]]In the south-east of the city (3 buildings to the right of the Pokécenter) is a building with a machine that can read a Pokémon's Individual Values (IVs) for a price of ₽1,000.
{{Clear}}

===Incredible Ball Man===
[[File:IncredibleBallGuy.png|thumb|Incredible Ball Man's shop]]Behind the gym in the alley to the right of the Northern gate is the [[#Shops|Incredible Ball Man's shop]]. His assistant will sell [[List of Pokéballs|Pokéballs]] with a variety of effects, however to unlock each in the shop the player must complete the Incredible Ball Man's [[Quests|quests]].
{{Clear}}

=== Dragon Pulse Move Tutor ===
On the second floor of the building eastern building near the Poké Mart is an Ace Trainer who will teach [[bulbapedia:Dragon Pulse (move)|Dragon Pulse]] to the player's Pokémon for {{P$}}4,000.

=== Drain Punch Move Tutor ===
In the Pokémon Center, after clearing [[Silph Co. Head Office|Silph Co.]] is a Battle Girl who will teach [[bulbapedia:Drain Punch (move)|Drain Punch]] to the player's Pokémon for {{P$}}2,000.

=== Comet Shard Collector ===
In the Pokémon Center, after clearing [[Silph Co. Head Office|Silph Co.]] is a man who will purchase a {{ItemIcon|COMETSHARD}} Comet Shard for {{P$}}120,000. This exchange can be repeated.

=== Chuck Rematch ===
After clearing [[Mt. Silver]], Chuck can be found in front of the Fighting Dojo during the [[Time|afternoon]]. After talking to him, he will appear at the Fighting Arena in [[Vermillion City]] for a [[Gym Leader rematches|rematch]].

